            <ArticleTitle>Successful closure of a coronary vessel rupture with a vein graft stent: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>172-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a successfully percutaneous closure of a brisk coronary artery rupture with a custom-made &quot;vein graft stent,&quot; a Palmaz-Schatz stent covered with a vein graft. This method is an elegant and effective alternative to the traditional surgical approach and should be considered whenever technically and clinically feasible.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
